e_accruals":-0.14707462512576058,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":83.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.21356491385112356,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":53.3,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.01792148556017828,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.1504384232111545,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":8.101467212312915,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.12524720213533994,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.03430845686098816,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":7.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.008532313477217956,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":41.5,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03265927631712785,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":47.4,"_gate_share_shrink":0.056663230808160936,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00818576455289528,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.01862,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":12.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Green Plains Inc. produces low-carbon fuels in the United States and internationally. It operates in two segments, Ethanol Production, and Agribusiness and Energy Services. The company produces, stores, and transports ethanol, distiller grains, and ultra-high protein and renewable corn oil. It is also involved in the grain procurement and commodity marketing businesses; and marketing ethanol for a third-party producer, as well as buys and sells ethanol, distiller grains, renewable corn oil, grain, natural gas, and other commodities in various markets. In addition, the company provides grain drying and storage services to grain producers. The company was formerly known as Green Plains Renewable Energy, Inc. and changed its name to Green Plains Inc. in May 2014. Green Plains Inc. was incorporated in 2004 and is headquartered in Omaha, Nebraska.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chris G. Osowski | President, CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 642 people. Revenue per employee of $3.3M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $115K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $27K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Green Plains, Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $941M market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -17% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 5% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $74M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (20.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 79/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Basic Materials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 40% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Critical Review: Green Plains (NASDAQ:GPRE) & Permian Resources (NYSE:PR)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thel